2026-10-20 | Flake fix -- R-02 drift gauge spec | 'fills the drift gauge while drifting' failed about half the time on main 2b14388 ('drift gauge stayed empty while drifting'). Cause, measured in the browser (HUD sampled every frame) and in a headless sim of the same inputs: the player starts on the left of the grid (lateral -4.5 m) on a straight; a held left drift turns the kart at about 3.8 rad/s and hits the left wall about 0.5 s of game time in; a steep hit (loss > 0.4) cancels the drift and zeroes the charge, as designed. The single read after 1.2 s sampled after that hit and passed only when frame stalls or a shallow scrape kept the drift alive. Not a game bug | The spec now polls #h-drift every 50 ms during the same 1.2 s drift window, keys still held, assertion unchanged (not '0%'). Game time never runs ahead of the wall clock (frame step capped at 50 ms), so a drift that lasts at least 0.5 s cannot fall between polls. The spec itself is the Tier-3 test. Verified: spec 10/10 consecutive, full e2e 37/37, typecheck and unit tests green | e2e/game.spec.ts
2026-10-20 | Flake fix -- team race start (DEC-020) | 'an account hosts, a guest joins...' failed 3/3 on main 2b14388: '#h-center' never showed 'PARTEZ !'. Measured with a frame recorder in both browsers: right after start both clients render no frame for 4-8 s (scene build, then shader compilation in the first draw) while the server's countdown runs on, so they come back after the green light and catch up without drawing it. A real bug for slow devices, not only a test issue. Polling alone, light graphics and a smaller viewport did not fix it (spec-only attempts failed 3 times in 2 batches) | Server: race-worker.js holds the clock (no step, no snapshot) until every human slot has sent its first input, capped by 'hold' (10 s default, runRace option); fast mode and all-AI grids start at once; a leaving driver stops counting. Client: netrace.js sends controls only from the second frame, after the first draw. Spec: both screens polled at once every 50 ms; assertion unchanged, default graphics kept. Tests: race.test.js +2 (hold, cap; the hold test fails without the fix), existing real-time test's Bob now sends idle controls as a client does; netrace.test.js asserts nothing is sent before the first draw. Verified: spec 10/10 in separate runs, full e2e 37/37, typecheck and unit tests green | apps/server/src/{race-worker,race,race.test}.js, apps/game/src/engine/{netrace,netrace.test}.js, e2e/multiplayer.spec.ts, .claude/DECISIONS.md
